To simplify the complex issue of cross-lingual transfer in NLP, we've redefined task representations and developed a model-agnostic approach using neural task representations as weak guidance. Our method achieves successful transfers without needing task-specific architectures or adaptation modules. We've tested it on three challenging cross-lingual datasets, and with minimal tuning, it has produced notable results, surpassing current standards in its field. What's more, we've shown that incorporating additional supervision enhances the transfer quality and opened up new avenues for exploration in the field of cross-lingual transfer. The code for this research is publicly available at https://github.com/ashwinkt/NTTask.ERP. Additionally, we've released the neural task representation library at https://github.com/ashwinkt/NTRep. It contains a range of neural task representations that can be utilized by other researchers. We believe our work has the potential to significantly contribute to the advancement of cross-lingual transfer in NLP. 

